From 6372a7601cd8641e25acc69387333f31ad5307d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:25:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] feat(deploy): add the gateway, service accounts and
 network policies

The Kubernetes manifests only deployed the control plane: there was no
gateway, the pod ran under the namespace's default service account and
nothing restricted who could reach it, so every workload in the cluster
could call the control plane directly.

gateway-deployment.yaml adds the gateway Deployment and Service. It
shares the forgemesh-api-keys Secret, reaches the control plane through
its Service, uses /readyz and /healthz as probes (the readiness timeout
is longer than the gateway's own 2 second upstream check) and runs with
the same hardening as the control plane: non-root, read-only root file
system, no capabilities, RuntimeDefault seccomp. Both components now
run under dedicated service accounts without a mounted token, since
neither calls the Kubernetes API, and with enableServiceLinks off: a
Service named forgemesh would inject FORGEMESH_PORT=tcp://... and the
control plane would fail to start.

network-policies.yaml denies all traffic in the namespace by default
and then allows DNS for every pod, only the gateway to reach the
control plane on 8080, and any source to reach the gateway on 8081;
the gateway may only connect to the control plane. Probes and kubectl
exec, cp and port-forward are not affected, so the documented backup
and restore still works.

With a runtime launcher the inference instances listen on ephemeral
ports inside the control plane pod. launcher/network-policy.yaml lets
the gateway reach that port range, and launcher/fake-runtime-patch.yaml
turns on the inventory (from a ConfigMap) and the fake launcher, which
advertises the pod IP because the Service only forwards 8080.

Validated on kind with Calico 3.33 in nftables mode: with the policies
an authenticated request through the gateway succeeds and the 401 path
works, while pods in another namespace (including one labelled as the
gateway) and other pods in the namespace time out on the control plane
and the instance port; the fake launcher trial reaches Ready and
streams a chat through the gateway once the launcher policy is applied.
